  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social protection measures</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia and Tonga agreed to specific reforms of the national social protection system as part of budget support policy dialogue. In FY25, the Government of Tonga increased transfer values of both the elderly and disability benefit schemes and lowered of the age of eligibility of the elderly scheme from age 70 to age 67. In this reporting period, 8,221 people benefitted from social protection programs in Tonga where 55% were women and 45% were men, up 1,004 in the previous year.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic policy reform and management and private sector development</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Policy and technical advice provided in this reporting period to the Public Service Commission (PSC) to update policies related to overtime for public servants. This was based on recommendation from a wage bill analysis also provided in previous reporting periods as technical advice provided by DFAT.  The overtime policy limits claimable overtime hours and has been in place since December 2022.  This work has been largely backed by DFAT funded long term adviser placed within PSC.  This work is contributing to an easing of Government of Tonga&apos;s (GoT)  wage bill pressures and to effectively implement government policies that targets efficiency.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
